    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "The Venn diagram below shows the number of students speaking French and Italian in a classroom of 80 students.\n\nFirst find the missing information, then find the probability that a randomly chosen student:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p42-q3-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 42 p42-q3-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm,line width=0.8pt,text=black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw (0,0) rectangle (70,47);\n\\draw (24,26) circle (18);\n\\draw (46,26) circle (18);\n\\node at (20,32) {Italian};\n\\node at (51,32) {French};\n\\node at (20,20) {15};\n\\node at (51,20) {35};\n\\node[anchor=west] at (1,4) {Neither $=21$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 70,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
